// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO5/6/7 (dedicated onboard MAX98357A I2S
// amplifier bus) and GPIO10/11/12/13 (dedicated onboard microSD SPI bus).
// SPI2 (GPIO38/39/40/41, "for public usage" per vendor comment) stays
// available.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO47 tagged "led_high" (status LED labeled 'IO47', confirmed
// via yellobyte/YB-ESP32-S3-AMP README + schematic sheet 1/2 "Status LED
// (GPIO47)" section: GPIO47 -> LED -> R7 5k1 -> GND, i.e. LED lights when
// GPIO47 is driven HIGH). Same pin doubles as DAC_MUTE control (solder bridge,
// default open) per vendor pins_arduino.h comment - no conflict, still a real
// GPIO47-driven LED. GPIO0 "BOOT" pushbutton NOT tagged - vendor README
// documents it only as "shorts GPIO0 to ground... force the board into boot
// mode" (combined with reset button), not as a general-purpose user button -
// left for human review, see notes.txt.
